      },
      "rules": [
        {
          "body": "Apply when immediate document writes become reusable trailing work, document buffers outlive visible subscriptions, and save callbacks can synchronously navigate. Confirm any departure deadline separately. README.md: \"A workspace document buffer persists independently of the current view badge. Save callbacks can synchronously navigate.\"",
          "category": "applicability",
          "id": "R01"
        },
        {
          "body": "Bind accepted edits to their originating document's reusable trailing task, replace pending text, restart the quiet interval on every edit, and preserve the no-current-view guard. TASK: \"Coalesce edits using the existing trailing-task utility: after a 120 ms quiet\ninterval, write only the latest text in that editing burst. Subsequent bursts\nmust continue to save.\" src/coordinator.js: \"trailing(env.timers,120,text=>env.store.write(id,text))\" and \"edit(text){const view=getView();if(view){env.store.write(view.id,text);}}\". src/services.js: \"push(text) { if (ticket !== null) timers.cancel(ticket); value = text; ticket = timers.schedule(flush, wait); },\"",
          "category": "event_relation",
          "id": "R02"
        },
        {
          "body": "Clear the consumed batch before invoking callback-capable saving, preserving new edits queued by synchronous callback reentry. Preserve empty text as valid work; do not replace the null check with a truthiness check or clear pending work after the callback. src/services.js: \"const flush = () => { const saved = value; retire(); if (saved !== null) consume(saved); };\"",
          "category": "event_relation",
          "id": "R03"
        },
        {
          "body": "Separate persistent document work from subscription cleanup. View retirement must not discard accepted edits or destroy reusable per-document tasks. docs/host-api.md: \"Document buffers are owned by a separate BufferBank service, while Badge owns only a live subscription.\" Survival does not alone mandate immediate flushing on departure; establish any such deadline independently.",
          "category": "preservation",
          "id": "R04"
